  <h2>How we scored</h2>
  <p>
    We ranked the most-used free BMI calculators on four axes, each scored 1–10:
  </p>

  <ol>
    <li><strong>Accuracy</strong> — does it use the correct WHO formula? Does it handle metric and imperial properly? Are the cutoffs aligned with current guidelines?</li>
    <li><strong>Privacy</strong> — does it send your height and weight to a server? Does it set tracking cookies? Does it require an account?</li>
    <li><strong>UX / Clarity</strong> — is the result easy to find and interpret? Does it show the healthy range, category, and category meaning? Does it explain the limits of BMI?</li>
    <li><strong>Feature set</strong> — does it support both metric and imperial? Multiple BMI formulas (adult, child, senior, Asian)? Body-fat % cross-reference?</li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    Final ranking weights: Accuracy 30%, Privacy 30%, UX 25%, Features 15%. We deliberately weight privacy heavily
